{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>The nesher</b> — He began with the nesher because it is king among birds, as stated: 'If you exalt yourself like the nesher' (אם על פיך יגביה נשר). If you take [it as] ס\"ת — king."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The phrase 'אם על פיך יגביה נשר' appears to be a abbreviated/defective quotation of Obadiah 1:4 ('אם תגביה כנשר משם אורידך נאם יהוה'); the citation formula 'שנ׳' introduces it. The label ס\"ת likely signals a notarikon or acronym reading; translated literally as 'If you take [it as] ס״ת — king.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:43.760238325Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}